==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_CareTeamGating  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_CareTeamGating.als
    rationale: Removing F_CareTeamGating allows the model to produce a Permitted outcome on a RecordLookup or AddNote operation where no ActiveMembership links the caller to the patient. This directly contradicts the care-team ownership invariant (FR-004) and the NoInformationLeakage assertion that denied paths never yield Permitted.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_004_CareTeamGating, NoInformationLeakage
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_004_CareTeamGating: PASS (vacuous?)
      - NoInformationLeakage: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AdminRestrictedToListAudit  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_AdminRestrictedToListAudit.als
    rationale: Removing F_AdminRestrictedToListAudit allows the model to construct a HospitalAdministrator Operation with opKind = RecordLookup, violating the role-separation invariant. LeastPrivilege will find a counterexample because an admin reaches a clinical endpoint.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_005_AdminRestrictedToListAudit, FR_018_AdminNoClinicaContent
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_005_AdminRestrictedToListAudit: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_018_AdminNoClinicaContent: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditOperationBijection  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_AuditOperationBijection.als
    rationale: Removing F_AuditOperationBijection allows two distinct Operations to share the same AuditEntry, breaking the one-to-one invariant. AuditCompleteness and FR_014_AuditImmutable both assert uniqueness and completeness of the audit-to-operation mapping.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_012_AlwaysOnAudit, FR_014_AuditImmutable
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_012_AlwaysOnAudit: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_014_AuditImmutable: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_NoteCreatedOnlyForPermittedAddNote  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_NoteCreatedOnlyForPermittedAddNote.als
    rationale: Removing F_NoteCreatedOnlyForPermittedAddNote allows a ClinicalNote to be linked as opNoteCreated on a Denied or RecordLookup operation. This violates the append-only invariant and the validation-before-mutation invariant: a note would exist without a permitting operation.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_011_NotesAppendOnly, ValidationBeforeMutation
      - AppendOnly: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_011_NotesAppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - ValidationBeforeMutation: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditNoteRefConstraint  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_AuditNoteRefConstraint.als
    rationale: Removing F_AuditNoteRefConstraint allows an AuditEntry with access_type=list_audit or a denied add_note to carry a non-null aeNoteRef, or a permitted add_note to carry no aeNoteRef. FR_013_AuditEntryShape directly checks this structural rule; FR_015_AuditAtomicWithAccess requires the ref to exist on success.
    expected to FAIL: FR_013_AuditEntryShape, FR_015_AuditAtomicWithAccess
      - FR_013_AuditEntryShape: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_015_AuditAtomicWithAccess: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_ClinicalRolesCannotAccessListAudit  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_ClinicalRolesCannotAccessListAudit.als
    rationale: Removing F_ClinicalRolesCannotAccessListAudit allows a Doctor (or other clinical role) to have an Operation with opKind = ListAudit, breaching the administrator-exclusive audit endpoint invariant. FR_017_AdminOnlyListAudit will immediately find a counterexample.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_017_AdminOnlyListAudit, NoInformationLeakage
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_017_AdminOnlyListAudit: FAIL (expected)
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)

